# Line endings.
#
# The .env.example in this repository was committed with CRLF line endings, so a
# copy of it becomes a CRLF .env on the deployment host. Docker Compose strips the
# trailing CR, so containers keep working and the problem stays invisible -- but
# every shell script that reads the file breaks, because each value silently ends
# in a carriage return:
#
#   eval "$(grep -E '^POSTGRES_USER=' .env)"    # -> role "postgres\r" does not exist
#
# Pinning eol=lf keeps these files LF in the working tree on every platform,
# including Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true.
.env.example text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
gradlew      text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher must keep CRLF.
*.bat        text eol=crlf
